  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Mantech Advanced Systems International obligated $789M in FY2026 to date. Mantech received 122 awards so far this fiscal year and recorded an average award size of $6.5M. Obligations are down 21.4% year over year. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $433M, followed by the Department of Defense at $251M and the Department of State at $41.7M. Work is concentrated in Computer Systems Design Services at $412M, All Other Support Activities for Transportation at $142M, and Engineering Services at $134M. Historical totals show variation: FY21 obligations were $901M, FY22 were $1.1B, FY23 were $884M, FY24 were $1.2B, and FY25 were $1B, placing the FY2026 to date total below several prior years. The mix of agencies and NAICS markets shows a portfolio dominated by civilian IT and systems work with meaningful Department of Defense exposure. The fiscal year to date totals are partial and represent contract obligations unless otherwise noted.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers of Mantech Advanced Systems International in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $433M. The Department of Defense obligated $251M, the Department of State obligated $41.7M, and other buyers include the Department of the Interior at $20.4M and the Department of Commerce at $15.2M. Remaining notable buyers are the Department of Homeland Security at $12.8M, the Department of Justice at $6.8M, the Department of Energy at $4.7M, and the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau at $3.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and capabilities generate Mantech Advanced Systems International's obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services generated $412M in obligations. All Other Support Activities for Transportation produced $142M and Engineering Services produced $134M. Additional markets include Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services at $30.7M, Custom Computer Programming Services at $23.6M, and Testing Laboratories and Services at $20.6M, with smaller amounts in related computer and R&D categories."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Mantech Advanced Systems International make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Mantech Advanced Systems International obligated $789M in FY2026 to date across federal contracts. Mantech received 122 awards so far this fiscal year, the average award size was $6.5M, and obligations are down 21.4% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Mantech Advanced Systems International?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $433M. The Department of Defense obligated $251M, the Department of State obligated $41.7M, the Department of the Interior obligated $20.4M, and the Department of Commerce obligated $15.2M. Other buyers include the Department of Homeland Security at $12.8M, the Department of Justice at $6.8M, the Department of Energy at $4.7M, and the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau at $3.4M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Mantech Advanced Systems International sell to the government?",
      "a": "Mantech Advanced Systems International sells largely IT and technical services, led by Computer Systems Design Services at $412M. Other significant markets are All Other Support Activities for Transportation at $142M and Engineering Services at $134M, with additional work in consulting, custom programming, testing laboratories, other computer services, and R&D markets."
    },
